From d4dd6fc179ddf3af2f6cf8f2c065fee773bf514e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kaaz <nk6352@stellar-intel.princeton.edu>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:44:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Raise MAXSCAT 2000 -> 200000 to stop discarding
 thick-wind photons

trans_phot.c terminates any photon reaching MAXSCAT scatters with
P_TOO_MANY_SCATTERS and discards its energy. The tau_es~100 photon-tired
winds need ~50k scatters per photon to escape, so the upstream default of
2000 destroyed ~94% of the luminosity: photon fates for pt_m5 were
escape=332 / too_many_scatters=1650 (vs escape=6730 / too_many=0 with the
cap raised), giving a 20x too-faint spectrum and starving the radiation
field enough to drive spurious recombination.

This is independent of the Lya-trapping feature it was previously bundled
with; the photon-tired production runs need it on its own merits. The
marginally-unbound winds peak at ~1200 scatters and are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/sirocco.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/sirocco.h b/source/sirocco.h
index 53979472..4a8efd24 100644
--- a/source/sirocco.h
+++ b/source/sirocco.h
@@ -141,7 +141,13 @@ extern int NWAVE_NOW;         /**< Either NWAVE_IONIZ or NWAVE_EXTRACT depending
                                 */
 #define NWAVE_MIN   100       /**< The minimum number of wavelength bins in during spectral cycles
                                */
-#define MAXSCAT    2000
+#define MAXSCAT    200000     /**< Photons reaching this many scatters are destroyed by
+                                 trans_phot.c (P_TOO_MANY_SCATTERS), discarding their energy.
+                                 The tau_es~100 photon-tired winds need ~50k scatters per
+                                 photon to escape, so the upstream default of 2000 silently
+                                 destroys ~94% of the luminosity. Check the diagnostic
+                                 "luminosity lost by too many scatters" is 0 on thick winds.
+                                 */
 
 /* Define the structures */
 #include "math_struc.h"
